thcare faces significant challenges including data privacy (HIPAA compliance), bias in training data, regulatory uncertainty, and integration with existing systems.\n    30→\n    31→## The Path Forward\n    32→\n    33→The future likely involves AI and human expertise working together. Rather than replacing doctors, AI will augment medical professionals by handling routine diagnostic tasks, flagging unusual cases for specialist review, suggesting treatment options based on latest research, and monitoring patient outcomes to improve care.\n    34→\n    35→Healthcare organizations are beginning to invest seriously in AI infrastructure. According to recent surveys, 60% of healthcare systems are exploring or implementing AI solutions, up from 30% just three years ago.\n    36→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
